(defmodule shells
  "**The program buffers you type into** — a line-oriented program's input region (comint),
the project shell and Brood REPL, and the terminal.

The context's details live under `src/shells/`: the input region every line-oriented buffer
shares (`shells/comint`), the project shell (`shells/bshell`, C-x p e) and the terminal
(`shells/terminal`, C-x p t, C-x p r). It sits on the editing commands and on the
`processes` context. Other code reaches it through its commands, by name, and the functions
below — a package's own terminal session (`term-run`), what a line buffer holds as typed
input, and the live sessions a quit asks about. The terminal stays DEFERRED (it pulls in std's `vt`): a
delegate loads its target on its first call, so loading this module loads neither.")

(defdelegate term-run (m label root command) shells/terminal)
(defdelegate input-text (buffer) shells/comint)
(defdelegate term-live (m) shells/terminal)
(defdelegate bshell-live (m) shells/bshell)
